# The line gpio_echo reads and the line it drives. On the classic ESP32 the defaults are the
# [lines.modem] set of the lilygo-t-a7670g-r2 board profile: RI, which the board pulls down, and
# PWRKEY. On the ESP32-S3, ESP32-C3 and ESP32-C6 they are the [lines.echo] set of the chip's
# devkit profile (esp32-s3-devkitc, esp32-c3-devkitm, esp32-c6-devkitc): GPIO 6 in, 7 out.
menu "gpio_echo"

config GPIO_ECHO_IN_PIN
    int "Input GPIO: the line gpio_echo reads"
    range 0 39
    default 33 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
    default 6
    help
        Read with the chip's own pulls off: an undriven line reads what the board's
        wiring gives it. Not the console's UART0 pins, nor the SPI flash's, nor a GPIO
        the chip does not have (on the classic ESP32: 1, 3, 6 to 11, 20, 24, 28 to 31):
        the range cannot leave them out.

config GPIO_ECHO_OUT_PIN
    int "Output GPIO: the line gpio_echo drives to the input's level"
    range 0 33
    default 4 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
    default 7
    help
        Not the console's UART0 pins, nor the SPI flash's, nor a GPIO the chip does not
        have (on the classic ESP32: 1, 3, 6 to 11, 20, 24, 28 to 31): the range cannot
        leave them out.

endmenu
